+# V31 additive preparation registration
+
+No existing reset/step, command/log interface, planner, physical transition, M/C defaults or evaluation function changed. C02 all858 scientific files and36 inputs are required unchanged; six scientific files are added (four module files, one registry and one targeted test file). AGENTS and documentation changes are scope records, outside the scientific source binding.
+
+New public entry: python -B -m tools.model_closeout_v31.validation --list; --case <one of four registered IDs> --output <fresh D/E child>. No arbitrary policy/hardware override or new offline schedule argument. Internal alias remains M; execution policy IDs are M_cooling_permission_v31 / M_steam_permission_v31 and display/method identities are explicit in CASE/RESULT/INVOCATION.
+
+Cooling retains the ordinary V30 terminal adapter and actual M23 controller, with only cooling_preparation=True. Current-only summary cooling_constraints_active=False is not proof that the healthy_converter_permission layer did not run; inspect actual solver layers and permissions.
+
+Steam adapter creates an opt-in mixin of the unchanged current EngineeringCore class before normal reset. The M23 policy subclass first delegates the complete unchanged M/M22 current-witness decision, then copies only current three boiler availability features and their existing provenance clocks plus the immutable total rating to a per-factory mailbox. reset_policy_memory clears the mailbox; each formal run uses its own fresh factory/episode/process. No observation, witness, solve or event-table read is added by the preparation hook. The mixin delegates shared preparation first, then changes only boiler_steam_lbph; metadata is added at joint_dispatch.diagnostic.v31_steam_permission. Physical model_config has no new capacities or strategy switches.
+
+Trace fields contain original planner ceiling, common minimum-prepared ceiling, new ceiling, current observable capacity/rating, feature clocks, generation minute and rule basis. Actual arrival minute is read offline from the original command_generated / command_arrived events joined by ID; the online rule does not learn a future release time. Actual readiness/steam/stock remain independent native evidence. Availability is model-observable current health, not OEM qualification or completed startup.
+
+Targeted TDD actual RED:14 missing-feature failures. First GREEN attempt:13 passed/1 test harness AttributeError, because an intentionally small plant stub omitted existing M23 converter/tower ratings. The harness was replaced by the unchanged real load_plant fixture; no production code, capacity, service criterion or assertion tolerance was relaxed. Final local14 and combined60 tests passed; original logs and commands remain in E:/hospital_ies_v31_20261027/steps. The60 count includes the14; do not add them to manufacture74. Historical1363 remains V30 provenance and was not rerun this round.
